**How to implement.** The app reads the limit from `appsettings.json` and carries it in the workbench settings (001 §F 'up to `KitHistoryLimit` = 100 folders (`appsettings.json`)'; 001 §G 'Every path is overridable in appsettings.json'; the S5.1 brief: a ConfigKey in AppConfig.fs with a settings door, carried in WorkbenchSettings). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`: the `WorkbenchSettings` record (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:87-93`) gains `kitHistoryLimit : KitHistoryLimit` (step 162) as its last field, and `defaults` (`:95-101`) gains `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`; the record's doc adds the kit history limit's 100 to the built-in values it says are written once here. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`. (a) Module `ConfigKey` gains `[<Literal>] let kitHistoryLimit = "KitHistoryLimit"` after `thicknessBucketCap`, its doc one line: the appSettings int of 001 §F, the most kits the history keeps, default 100 (`KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`). (b) Module `WorkbenchSettingsDoors` (`AppConfig.fs:64-109`): the three count doors (`QuickPickThreshold`, `TreeAutoBuildThreshold`, `ThicknessBucketCap`) repeat one body today: an invariant-culture `Int32.TryParse`, the type's own int `tryCreate`, and the refusals `not a positive count: '<text>'` and `not a whole number: '<text>'`. That body moves to ONE private extension member of STL's `AppSettings.ConfigValue` declared in this module, `member private this.tryPositiveCount (create : int -> Result<'Setting, WorkbenchSettingsError>) : Result<'Setting, string>`, and the three doors call it, their answers and texts unchanged. `type KitHistoryLimit with` gains the same door: `static member tryCreate (v : AppSettings.ConfigValue) : Result<KitHistoryLimit, string>` through `tryPositiveCount`, and `member this.configValue : AppSettings.ConfigValue` rendering the count as the other doors do. The shared member is private, so it adds no public signature mixing our types with primitives (ELEV010), and no fourth copy of the body is written (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). (c) `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) builds the record with `kitHistoryLimit = readSetting provider (AppSettings.ConfigKey ConfigKey.kitHistoryLimit) defaults.kitHistoryLimit KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate _.configValue` beside the other keys, so a missing or refused key is logged and written back as 100 by `readSetting` (`AppConfig.fs:117`), and it is saved with them once. A doc that counts the keys it reads stops counting them. The limit's reader is `KitHistory.bump` (step 169), which takes it as a parameter. (3) Census only: the record's other consumers, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs` and the Ui.Tests files `AppContextTests.fs`, `LauncherTests.fs`, `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs`, `WindowLauncherTests.fs`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiCompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`, read the record or its `defaults` and build no literal of it, so nothing in them changes; they are in scope so the shape change covers its whole census. Every reader a later step added (`TestAppScope.fs`, step 83) is likewise unchanged. (4) Tests. In `OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs`, `defaults equals the record constructed directly from the per-type defaults` (`WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs:22-30`) builds its record with `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, and `a settings record assembled from validated values carries the validated thresholds` (`:96-116`) with `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate 250 |> okOr KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue` and asserts 250; `the default settings carry a kit history limit of 100` is added: `WorkbenchSettings.defaults.kitHistoryLimit` is `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, whose value is 100. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs` (step 82), `the count doors read a positive whole number and refuse anything else, the kit history limit's included`: with `OpticalConstructor.App` open, `KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate (AppSettings.ConfigValue "250")` answers a limit of 250 whose `configValue` is `"250"`; `"0"` answers `Error "not a positive count: '0'"` and `"ten"` answers `Error "not a whole number: 'ten'"`; and `QuickPickThreshold.tryCreate`, `TreeAutoBuildThreshold.tryCreate` and `ThicknessBucketCap.tryCreate` of `"0"` and of `"ten"` answer those same two texts, so the one body serves all four doors.

**Acceptance.** After the limit is read from `appsettings.json`, `WorkbenchSettings.defaults.kitHistoryLimit` MUST be 100, `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings` MUST read the `KitHistoryLimit` key through its door, and the four count doors MUST share one parse body; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default settings carry a kit history limit of 100`, `defaults equals the record constructed directly from the per-type defaults` and `a settings record assembled from validated values carries the validated thresholds`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the count doors read a positive whole number and refuse anything else, the kit history limit's included`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.
